<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gobir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gobir was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> kingdom in present-day north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, and the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usman-dan-fodio">Usman dan Fodio</a>. Its sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunfa">Yunfa</a>'s hostility to dan Fodio triggered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a> of 1804, and the storming of the Gobir capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alkalawa">Alkalawa</a> in 1808 consolidated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
